  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The music of the sentence",
     "texto": [
      "Vietnamese can't raise or lower the voice to show surprise or doubt, because the tone is already taken up by each word. That job is done by some **little words at the end**. You've been seeing them; here they all are together:",
      "**ạ** = respect: «Vâng **ạ**». **nhé / nha** = okay?, seeks agreement: «Mai gặp **nhé**».",
      "**nhỉ** = right?, eh? (you think aloud, asking to be agreed with): «Trời đẹp **nhỉ**».",
      "**à / hả / hử** = ah, yes?, really? (confirming with surprise): «Cậu về rồi **à**?».",
      "**chứ** = of course; …, right?: «Đi **chứ**!».",
      "**mà** = it's just that…, I already told you (insists or protests): «Tớ đã bảo rồi **mà**!».",
      "**cơ** = no less; but rather (corrects towards more, or towards something else): «Hai mươi cái **cơ**?» = Twenty, no less? «Tớ thích cái kia **cơ**» = No, I want that one.",
      "**đấy** = just so you know, mind (warns or stresses): «Nóng **đấy**!».",
      "**đâu** = not at all (reinforces a no): «Không khó **đâu**».",
      "**thôi** = only, and that's it: «Một chút **thôi**». **vậy** = well then, there's no choice: «Thôi, đi **vậy**».",
      "They combine: **cơ mà** (but surely…, it's just that…), **đấy nhé** (mind you, eh?), **thôi mà** (come on, leave it), **chứ nhỉ** (don't you think?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
